    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1159">

                <pb facs="1006" n="902" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg902"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/57.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at
                            Chihuahua to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d1159-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Chihuahua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-12-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 11, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A considerable number of Spanish subjects will leave here tomorrow by train for
                    El Paso. I recommend that financial aid be requested <pb facs="1007" n="903"
                        xml:id="pg903"/> from Red Cross for relief at El Paso. If possible authority
                    is requested to issue letters of identification to Spanish subjects here for use
                    at border.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Letcher</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1159-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1159-f1-content">
                <p>Referred December 13 to the Secretaries of Labor and War, and the American
                    National Red Cross, for such action as may be deemed necessary.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
